  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 1217 PM MDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nBy Wednesday, the Monsoon high will be repositioned to over the\nGulf Coast and winds in the lower/mid levels of the atmosphere\nwill turn out of the south, transporting moisture north across NM\nand bringing PWATs back to near average for mid August. PWATs will\ncontinue to rise through the end of the work week as troughing\nalong the west coast allows for a continuous moisture feed into \nthe region. Temperatures will trend down and chances for showers \nand storms will trend up during the Wednesday through Saturday \nperiod, bringing a localized flash flooding threat that will be \nelevated on/near area burn scars. At this time, Friday and\nSaturday are forecast to be the two most active days of the next\nseven, with above average PWATs across the region. The upper high\nis modeled to build back to the west over NM late in the weekend \nand into early next week, bringing a slight uptrend in \ntemperatures and slight downtrend in rain chances.",
